6052	// Custom recon-solve kernels: replace the cuSOLVER trsm_right (L21) and trsm_l
6053	// (U12) calls in the orhr_col reconstruction. At batch=2 those cuSOLVER kernels
6054	// are SIMT and underfill the 148 SMs (only 2 matrices' tiles). The diagonal
6055	// block is tiny (w<=64) so a CTA inverts its U (upper, incl diagonal) and V
6056	// (unit-lower) triangles ONCE in smem -- parallel back/forward substitution over
6057	// the w columns (only w sequential steps, shared by all rows) -- then applies the
6058	// inverse to the wide L21/U12 panels as plain dot-product GEMMs spanning BOTH
6059	// matrices in one grid (blockIdx -> (row/col-tile, matrix)), filling the SMs.
6060	// Pre-inverting is strictly more parallel than a per-row forward-substitution
6061	// (latency-bound at b2): each output row
6062	// becomes w INDEPENDENT dot products instead of a w-deep dependency chain.
6063	// FP32 throughout (the recon's factor residual is loose, ~0.3 vs gate ~32, but
6064	// the LU is sequential so its inputs must stay exact; a TF32 inverse-GEMM
6065	// corrupts the V used by householder_product).
